<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE policyconfig PUBLIC
 "-//freedesktop//DTD PolicyKit Policy Configuration 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/PolicyKit/1.0/policyconfig.dtd">
<!--
  The Welcomer's privileged helper, authorized under its own action.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Every privileged path in the Welcomer runs a bare
  `pkexec <program>`. With no action registered for the program, polkit falls
  back to its generic org.freedesktop.policykit.exec action, and the prompt the
  user is shown says only that a program wants to run as another user. A first
  boot on an installed machine recorded exactly that fallback being refused:

    polkitd: Operator of unix-session:2 FAILED to authenticate to gain
             authorization for action org.freedesktop.policykit.exec
             for [the Welcomer]
    pkexec:  Error executing command as another user: Request dismissed

  Nothing was misconfigured — the prompt was dismissed. But a prompt that
  cannot say what it is for is a prompt a person is right to dismiss, and the
  generic action names neither the application nor the change.

  WHAT IT CHANGES, and what it does not. One action covers the whole helper,
  the same shape org.intergenos.intergen.policy uses for the privileged-tool
  tier: the helper takes a fixed set of verbs and validates its own arguments,
  so the authentication boundary is the helper, and the argument boundary is
  inside it. The strength is unchanged — auth_admin, the same as the generic
  exec action's own default — so this is a clearer prompt, not a weaker gate.

  auth_admin, NOT auth_admin_keep, and deliberately so: unlike the assistant's
  tool dispatch, these are a handful of one-off choices a person makes while
  reading a page, so there is no run of calls for a cached credential to cover,
  and each change to a system service or the machine's name servers is worth
  its own authentication.
-->
<policyconfig>
  <vendor>InterGenOS</vendor>
  <vendor_url>https://github.com/InterGenJLU/intergenos</vendor_url>
  <icon_name>preferences-system</icon_name>

  <action id="org.intergenos.welcome.configure-system">
    <description>Change a system service or the machine's name servers</description>
    <description xml:lang="en_US">Change a system service or the machine's name servers</description>
    <message>Authentication is required to apply the change you just chose in the InterGenOS Welcomer</message>
    <message xml:lang="en_US">Authentication is required to apply the change you just chose in the InterGenOS Welcomer</message>
    <defaults>
      <allow_any>auth_admin</allow_any>
      <allow_inactive>auth_admin</allow_inactive>
      <allow_active>auth_admin</allow_active>
    </defaults>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.path">/usr/libexec/intergen-welcome/intergen-welcome-privhelper</annotate>
    <annotate key="org.freedesktop.policykit.exec.allow_gui">true</annotate>
  </action>
</policyconfig>
